<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andrianjaka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 17th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andrianjaka was a king of Imerina in the central highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> in the early seventeenth century, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ralambo">Ralambo</a>. Tradition credits him with capturing the hill of Analamanga, which he renamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antananarivo">Antananarivo</a> and made the royal seat, and with acquiring firearms. He is remembered as one of the founders of the Merina kingdom.</p></div>
